KNOWNBUG: [except.ctor]/1-3, [except.throw]/4 -- an automatic object in an outer
scope that is exited because the exception does not match an inner handler is
not destroyed during unwinding.  The destructor-unwinding in goto-conversion
only unwinds up to the innermost enclosing try at the throw site, so `g` here is
never destroyed (assertion 2 currently FAILS, VERIFICATION FAILED).  Flip to
CORE once unwinding destroys every scope exited on the way to the handler.
